# Force LF everywhere, on every platform, regardless of a clone's local
# core.autocrlf setting. Not a stylistic preference -- this project spent
# real effort this session finding and fixing CRLF bugs that silently broke
# exact-match ID lookups and corrupted sequence data at the Windows/WSL
# boundary (see run_features.py's and several modules' own comments). A
# shell script checked out with CRLF doesn't just misbehave, it fails to
# execute at all ("bad interpreter" -- the shebang line becomes
# "#!/usr/bin/env bash\r"). Don't leave this to chance per-clone.
* text=auto eol=lf
